# Run the whole suite before anything reaches the remote.
#
# Here rather than in pre-commit because this is the boundary that matters:
# pushing to main deploys the site, so a broken push breaks production, while a
# broken local commit costs nothing and can be amended. Running once per push
# also beats once per commit.
#
# Not `jest --onlyChanged`: Jest builds its dependency graph from imports and
# cannot see readFileSync, so an edit to any .html file selects zero suites --
# even though __tests__/html.test.js checks every page and the game suites load
# their index.html that way. Nearly every commit here touches HTML.
npm test
